msgid "Committee review of a content change"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/content-change-review-committee.bpmn:184
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Committee reviews the agent's impact assessment: - Were all downstream effects identified? - Are the indicator changes acceptable? - Does the logic change match the narrative intent?"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/content-change-review-committee.bpmn:53
#. Diagram label
msgid "Compare main vs staging"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/content-change-review-committee.bpmn:24
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Compares staged against main, reviews the slices it is assigned (review-task.bpmn, one call per slice), takes a disputed finding to adjudication, judges the impact assessment, and decides. Task_Approve records the approval; merging is a separate, confirmed act in the publish phase. A rejection ends this phase with changes requested, and the caller routes it to Task_Iterate in the agent's lane rather than to the author."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/content-change-review-committee.bpmn:156
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Computed, not chosen: `decisions/review-coverage-gate.dmn` reads `uncoveredBlocks` (changed blocks with neither a verdict nor a reasoned waiver) and `openDefects`, and, where the build published a rendered impact, `unreviewedPages`, `undeterminedInputs` and `missedPages` with their `rendered` and `measured` statuses (skill rendered-impact). Resolved comments are not coverage, and coverage is not approval — that is GW_Approved."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/content-change-review-committee.bpmn:155
#. Diagram label
msgid "Every changed block and page reviewed?"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/content-change-review-committee.bpmn:83
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Every PR conversation comment that starts with `block: <label>` becomes a `review-comment/1.0.0` todo (open), idempotently, and is published with the preview as `review-comments.json`. The staging workflow runs this on every push and on every tagged comment; the coordinator owns that it has run before slicing, because the slices are cut around what reviewers have already said. This is the `ingest` transition of REVIEW_TRANSITIONS. Uses `folio-review-comments`."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/content-change-review-committee.bpmn:91
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "From the ChangeSet, its rendered list (skill rendered-impact: each changed rendered page is assigned like a changed block) and the heat map on the review page: cut the change into slices a reviewer can hold (usually a section, or a run of sections where the heat map clusters), and assign each slice to a review lane by what it contains — clinical content to a clinical SME, a decision table to a QC reviewer, prose to a narrative reviewer. A block that needs no review (a pure rename, say) is WAIVED here with a written reason, which is what the coverage gate counts. Re-entered from GW_Covered when coverage is incomplete: the uncovered blocks become new slices."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/content-change-review-committee.bpmn:82
#. Diagram label
msgid "Ingest tagged review comments"
msgstr ""

